      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    bid_rates = [6.2, 6.4, 6.1, 6.5, 6.3, 6.4, 6.0, 6.1]\n    offer_rates = [6.6, 6.7, 6.5, 6.8, 6.7, 6.8, 6.4, 6.5]\n\n    # Calculate and sort the mid-rates\n    mid_rates = [(bid + offer) / 2 for bid, offer in zip(bid_rates, offer_rates)]\n    mid_rates.sort()\n\n    # Remove the two lowest and two highest mid-rates\n    trimmed_mid_rates = mid_rates[2:-2]\n\n    # Calculate the JIBAR and round to two decimal places\n    jibar_rate = round(sum(trimmed_mid_rates) / len(trimmed_mid_rates), 2)\n\n    # Return the answer\n    return jibar_rate\n```",
